{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS2AYKinBQuVuTk5QXVR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found two stacked bugs and fixed both in the snapshot. I haven't run any of it, because launchd, `claude` and Telegram aren't available here.\n\n**Why it was silent**\n1. **The job did fire.** `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`, so it ran every night and failed. The `.err` log holds both causes below.\n2. **`claude -p` was \"Not logged in\".** The plist's `EnvironmentVariables` had only `PATH`, with no `USER` or `HOME`. Under launchd the CLI couldn't find its login in the keychain, so every run died immediately.\n3. **`status=$?` aborted the script.** In zsh `status` is read-only, so line 19 killed the script before the failure notification ran (\"read-only variable: status\"). The failure reporter sat downstream of the failure, which made it completely silent.\n\n**What I changed**\n- **`bin/nightly-review.zsh`:**\n  - It uses `rc=$?` instead of `status=$?`.\n  - `claude` now runs with `< /dev/null`.\n  - Empty output now counts as a failure.\n  - Exit code and duration go to stderr.\n  - A failed run always exits non-zero.\n- **The plist:** I added `USER` and `HOME`. You need to copy it to `~/Library/LaunchAgents` and reload it with `launchctl bootout` and `bootstrap`.\n\n`ANSWER.md` lists the causes and which parts of your colleague's note applied. The \"pipe the prompt via stdin\" fix didn't apply, since your prompt is an argument and the real error was the login. Their 16:50 schedule also differs from your 02:30 job.\n\n**To check on your machine**\n- Run `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`.\n- Confirm exit 0, a fresh non-empty output file, a run time longer than a few seconds, and a Telegram message.\n- Then break the script on purpose once to confirm the failure note arrives.\n- If \"Not logged in\" persists, the keychain may be unavailable to a background session. `notify.sh` uses the same keychain for the Telegram token, so it may need the same check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1690,"cache_read_input_tokens":24794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1690},"output_tokens":729,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"712a262c-b18b-49f1-a344-f8a0feb0b40d","uuid":"a0f36495-4894-4e4d-b7d2-c09f123fbdb3","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:20:05.836Z","request_id":"req_011CgS2AY2rb37my4M7FJ3eC"}
